    "todo": [
        "Final research 2026-10-28 (owner: no external review, docs/country-packs-research-2026-10.md): every value is used as researched; none blocks a run.",
        "inpp: from 2026-01-01 3.5% (1 to 50 employees), 3% (51 to 300), 2% (above 300), medium. The interministerial order is N°002/CAB/MET/2025, N°158/CAB/MIN/FINANCES/2025, N°003/CAB/VPM/MIN/BUD/2025 of 2025-09-24 (listed in the Journal officiel, in force on signature, repeals the 2006 order); its full text is behind a paywall, the rates come from PaySpace and Sage. Until 2025-12-31: 3/2/1% (low).",
        "cnss: the employee's 5% reduces the IPR base (PwC, reviewed April 2026; one calculator agrees, two disagree): low, used.",
        "ipr: from 2026-01-01 the tax is IRPP (Law 23/053): same bands, the monthly tax rounded to the nearest CDF 100. The CDF 2,000 minimum applies first and the 30% cap wins (order of operations kept; no source states it). Not applied: 'no rebate above the third band' (one source).",
        "ipr_dependants: 2% of the tax per dependant, at most 9 (PwC, Monrespro, Sage): medium, applied.",
        "family_allowance: 1/27 of the daily minimum wage per child per day, times 26 days (Decree 25/22 of 2025-05-30, art. 5; paid by the employer on the payslip). Daily minimum wage CDF 14,500 from 2025-05 (13,963 a month) and CDF 21,500 from 2026-01 (20,704 a month). Taxable and contributory are assumed true (part of the minimum remuneration, arts 87 and 96 of the Code; CNSS contributions cannot be exempted, Decree 18/027 art. 8). A ceiling of 6 children is cited as usual but not found in a text, so none is applied. Low.",
        "ipr and the contributions: rounding to the franc is assumed. cnss: no ceiling on the base (none found).",
        "onem: base is the taxable base (ANAPI).",
        "Not modelled: a minimum wage check, housing and transport allowance exemptions, an exceptional tax on expatriates' pay.",
        "non_monthly: how the monthly figures apply to weekly and bi-weekly pay; until then only monthly runs are calculated.",
        "returns: the IPR (DGI), CNSS, INPP and ONEM declaration layouts; until then return files are placeholders."
    ],
